WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.860
BETH: The internet and mobile phones
mean bullying can now happen during

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.310
the day, when an individual is
mixing with others and when they

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.910
are in the safety of their own home.

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:13.959
Online or cyber bullying can be
via text messages, emails, online

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.679
gaming, chat rooms, instant
messaging and social networks.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.390
Some autistic young people may need
extra support and guidance to stay

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.860
safe online and educational settings
have a duty and responsibility to

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.660
protect individuals in their care.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.759
JOE: If an individual is being bullied
either at school or at work, then

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.930
it’s best to talk to them and find
out more, to see if help can be given.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.870
They should be calmly listened to
making sure that they know they are

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.840
believed and it’s not their fault.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.680
Some individuals with autism will
find it easier to write about the

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.409
incident or draw a picture about
what happened, and they could be

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.809
encouraged to keep a diary of events.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.320
BETH: The individual may not realise
that they are being bullied and may need

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.570
this explained to them, differentiating
between being friendly or being a bully.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.780
They should be told why behaviour
that hurts or harms them

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.249
emotionally or physically, is
not acceptable and is bullying.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.839
JOE: An individual may show
sudden changes in behaviour,

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:12.470
which may be due to bullying.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.780
This might be increased anxiety,
difficulty sleeping or outbursts at home.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.880
A child may mimic the acts of bullies,
at home, by bullying their siblings

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.350
because they don't understand that this
behaviour is unacceptable, they are simply

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.490
acting out what their peers are doing.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.320
BETH: Sometimes an individual
with autism may bully others.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.270
This is more often not intentional
bullying, but a way of communicating

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.580
and trying to get attention.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.600
It may be because they are being
told to do it by others, exploiting

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.289
their need to fit in, and they may
be unaware of the consequences,

00:01:47.529 --> 00:01:48.890
and that they are hurting others.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:52.679
JOE: Discussing and showing them the
consequences of their actions can help

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.740
them to understand what they are doing
is wrong and maybe linking it to what has

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.070
been done to them can help to show this.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.939
BETH: The long-term effects of bullying
of individuals with autism can be

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:07.460
serious and they can end up with
long-lasting insecurities, behavioural

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.240
issues and low self-esteem, and
it can affect their concentration.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:15.930
They may become more inclined to refuse
to take part in social situations because

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.710
they are afraid of being bullied or they
may experience stress-related illnesses.

00:02:21.219 --> 00:02:24.710
JOE: If the bullying becomes really
serious and a potential criminal

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.050
offence is committed, it may be
necessary to contact the police.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.530
Harassment and stalking, threats of harm
or violence to a person or property,

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.430
evidence of sexual exploitation such as
grooming and the distribution of sexual

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:43.150
images or inappropriate sexual contact
or behaviour are all criminal offences.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:46.590
BETH: Addressing bullying issues as soon
as they are recognised and taking the

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.080
appropriate action, will help to reduce
the effects of bullying and exploitation

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.070
and hopefully reduce any long-term
issues that could be experienced.

